        "description": "Exclusion of other causes of hereditary spastic paraplegia",
        "category": "supportive",
        "requiredForDiagnosis": true
      },
      {
        "id": "neuroimaging-findings",
        "description": "MRI showing corticospinal tract degeneration or spinal cord atrophy",
        "category": "minor",
        "requiredForDiagnosis": false
      },
      {
        "id": "family-history",
        "description": "Consanguinity or affected siblings consistent with autosomal recessive inheritance",
        "category": "supportive",
        "requiredForDiagnosis": false
      }
    ],
    "minimumForDiagnosis": "Presence of progressive lower limb spasticity and weakness plus genetic confirmation of biallelic AP5Z1 pathogenic variants, with exclusion of other causes",
    "notes": "Genetic testing is essential for definitive diagnosis due to phenotypic overlap with other hereditary spastic paraplegias."
